{"name":"Pansy Garden","hex":"#7f8fca","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pansy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cultivated flowering plant, derived by hybridization within species Viola tricolor.","A deep purple colour, like that of the pansy."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Wimpy; spineless; feeble.","Of a deep purple colour, like that of the pansy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pansy"},{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pansy","blocks":[{"text":"The garden pansy is a type of polychromatic large-flowered hybrid plant cultivated as a garden flower. It is derived by hybridization from several species in the section Melanium of the genus Viola, particularly V. tricolor, a wildflower of Europe and western Asia known as heartsease. It is sometimes known as V. tricolor var. hortensis, but this scientific name is suspect. While V. tricolor var. hortensis Groenland & Rümpler is a synonym of Viola × wittrockiana, V. tricolor var. hortensis DC. refers to a horticultural variety of wild pansy that had been illustrated in Flora Danica in 1777 before the existence of Viola × wittrockiana."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/PansyScan_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-PansyScan_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pansy","wikidata":"Q12861234"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden","wikidata":"Q1107656"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Pansy_Flower.jpg/500px-Pansy_Flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Pansy_Flower.jpg/500px-Pansy_Flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pansy flower","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APansy_Flower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Purple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg/500px-Purple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Purple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg/500px-Purple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pansy displaying the two upper overlapping petals, the two side petals, and the single bottom petal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APurple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Pansy_bi_colour.jpg/500px-Pansy_bi_colour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Pansy_bi_colour.jpg/1280px-Pansy_bi_colour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedi